{
 "series": "Excel round",
 "style": "ember",
 "layout": "cards",
 "format": "list",
 "cover_bg": "mint",
 "cover_alt": {
  "title": "One formula counts unique names: ~SUMPRODUCT~",
  "hook": "one-sharp-fact",
  "bg": "yellow"
 },
 "slides": [
  {
   "type": "marker_cover",
   "title": "Excel round tomorrow? Practise these ~22~ tasks."
  },
  {
   "type": "sheet",
   "title": "~Lookups~ they always ask",
   "ribbon": "Find one value in a table",
   "tip": [
    "Interview trap:",
    "VLOOKUP only looks right. INDEX + MATCH looks any way."
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "name": "Region of order 103",
     "formula": "=VLOOKUP(103,A2:F8,3,FALSE)",
     "result": "North"
    },
    {
     "name": "Look left: Neha's order number",
     "formula": "=INDEX(A2:A8,MATCH(\"Neha Gupta\",B2:B8,0))",
     "result": "104"
    },
    {
     "name": "Missing order, no #N/A",
     "formula": "=IFERROR(VLOOKUP(999,A2:F8,3,FALSE),\"Not found\")",
     "result": "Not found"
    },
    {
     "name": "Sales of order 105",
     "formula": "=INDEX(A2:F8,MATCH(105,A2:A8,0),5)",
     "result": "950"
    }
   ],
   "data": "Example sheet, A2:F8 = Order, Rep, Region, City, Sales, Date. 7 orders (Apr to Jun 2024), order 104 entered twice, B2 is a messy name."
  },
  {
   "type": "sheet",
   "title": "~Conditional~ maths",
   "ribbon": "SUMIF, COUNTIF and friends",
   "tip": [
    "Say this:",
    "SUMIFS puts the sum range first. SUMIF puts it last."
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "name": "Total sales, North",
     "formula": "=SUMIF(C2:C8,\"North\",E2:E8)",
     "result": "4,200"
    },
    {
     "name": "Orders above 1,000",
     "formula": "=COUNTIF(E2:E8,\">1000\")",
     "result": "3"
    },
    {
     "name": "North sales from Kanpur only",
     "formula": "=SUMIFS(E2:E8,C2:C8,\"North\",D2:D8,\"Kanpur\")",
     "result": "3,000"
    },
    {
     "name": "Average South order",
     "formula": "=AVERAGEIF(C2:C8,\"South\",E2:E8)",
     "result": "875"
    },
    {
     "name": "Order 101 as % of total",
     "formula": "=ROUND(E2/SUM($E$2:$E$8)*100,1)",
     "result": "16.8"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "sheet",
   "title": "Clean messy ~text~",
   "ribbon": "Names from forms are never clean",
   "tip": [
    "Interview trap:",
    "TRIM removes extra spaces between words too, not only at the ends."
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "name": "Remove extra spaces",
     "formula": "=TRIM(B2)",
     "result": "ravi kumar"
    },
    {
     "name": "Fix the case too",
     "formula": "=PROPER(TRIM(B2))",
     "result": "Ravi Kumar"
    },
    {
     "name": "First name only",
     "formula": "=LEFT(B3,FIND(\" \",B3)-1)",
     "result": "Priya"
    },
    {
     "name": "City with region label",
     "formula": "=D2&\" (\"&C2&\")\"",
     "result": "Lucknow (North)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "sheet",
   "title": "~Dates~ without panic",
   "ribbon": "A date is a number underneath",
   "tip": [
    "Remember:",
    "Subtracting two dates gives days. Format the cell as a number."
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "name": "Month name",
     "formula": "=TEXT(F2,\"mmm\")",
     "result": "Apr"
    },
    {
     "name": "Month key for a pivot",
     "formula": "=TEXT(F2,\"yyyy-mm\")",
     "result": "2024-04"
    },
    {
     "name": "Days between two orders",
     "formula": "=F7-F2",
     "result": "78"
    },
    {
     "name": "Working days, Mon to Fri",
     "formula": "=NETWORKDAYS(F2,F3)",
     "result": "6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "sheet",
   "title": "The ~tricky~ ones",
   "ribbon": "Where most freshers get stuck",
   "tip": [
    "Interview trap:",
    "LARGE counts ties. Two orders of 1,500 make the 2nd highest 1,500 too."
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "name": "Flag the duplicate order",
     "formula": "=IF(COUNTIF($A$2:A8,A8)>1,\"Duplicate\",\"\")",
     "result": "Duplicate"
    },
    {
     "name": "Rank order 102 by sales",
     "formula": "=RANK(E3,$E$2:$E$8)",
     "result": "5"
    },
    {
     "name": "Second highest sale",
     "formula": "=LARGE(E2:E8,2)",
     "result": "1,500"
    },
    {
     "name": "Count unique reps (B3:B8)",
     "formula": "=SUMPRODUCT(1/COUNTIF(B3:B8,B3:B8))",
     "result": "3"
    },
    {
     "name": "Label each order",
     "formula": "=IF(E2>=1000,\"High\",IF(E2>=700,\"Mid\",\"Low\"))",
     "result": "High"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "bigtable",
   "title": "They also ask ~why~",
   "cols": [
    "#",
    "Question",
    "Short answer"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "VLOOKUP or INDEX + MATCH?",
     "INDEX + MATCH. It looks left and does not break when a column is added."
    ],
    [
     "Why FALSE at the end of VLOOKUP?",
     "Exact match. TRUE gives the nearest value and needs sorted data."
    ],
    [
     "What does $ do in $E$2?",
     "Locks the cell, so it stays fixed when you copy the formula."
    ],
    [
     "COUNT vs COUNTA?",
     "COUNT counts numbers. COUNTA counts every filled cell."
    ],
    [
     "SUMIF vs SUMIFS?",
     "SUMIF takes one condition. SUMIFS takes many, sum range first."
    ],
    [
     "Pivot did not update?",
     "Right click, Refresh. New rows need the source range or a Table."
    ],
    [
     "How do you remove duplicates?",
     "Data tab, Remove Duplicates. Flag them first with COUNTIF to check."
    ],
    [
     "Why does a date show 45385?",
     "Dates are numbers. Change the cell format to Date."
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "cta",
   "title": "Practise one page a ~day~.",
   "body": "Comment XLROUND and I'll DM you the full 9-page PDF.",
   "keyword": "XLROUND",
   "action": "Follow @thedataguy16"
  }
 ]
}